  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.65,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J1"],
      "pins": ["J1.SWDIO", "J1.SWCLK", "J1.SWO", "J1.RESET"],
      "nets": ["SWDIO", "SWCLK", "SWO", "NRST"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet (PCB.kicad_sch) the J1 Tag-Connect header has wires only to the VCC and GND power symbols; its four signal pins (the SWDIO, SWCLK, SWO and RESET pin names drawn inside the symbol body) have no wire and no global label, so they form isolated nets. The SWDIO/SWCLK/SWO labels exist only on U2 (PA13/PA14/PB3) and the NRST label only on U2 pin 7, none of which reach J1.",
      "expected": "J1 is the programming/debug interface; its SWDIO/SWCLK/SWO pins must share the MCU's SWDIO/SWCLK/SWO nets, and the spec explicitly states the reset line is connected: 'NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET}) so the Tag-Connect programmer can pull it low.'",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Its pins are VCC, GND, ~{RESET}, SWCLK, SWDIO, SWO — a standard ARM debug/programming interface"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "NRST is also wired to J1 pin 3 (~{RESET}) so the Tag-Connect programmer can pull it low"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "root sheet, 'Programming (SWD)' block: J1 shows green wires only from pin 1 (VCC) to a VCC symbol and pin 5 (GND) to a GND symbol; SWDIO/SWCLK/SWO/RESET pins carry no wire or label box"}
      ],
      "impact": "The Tag-Connect programmer cannot drive SWDIO/SWCLK/SWO or reset the MCU; the board cannot be programmed or debugged through J1.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U4"],
      "pins": ["U4.10"],
      "nets": ["VCC", "BS0"],
      "observed": "On the display sheet (display.kicad_sch) the BS0 pin (U4 pin 10) is wired into the same horizontal node that feeds the top of R4, R6 and R7 and the VCC power symbol (the VCC pull-up rail). Thus BS0 is held at VCC, and the BS1/BS2 straps are not the documented 0,1,0 combination.",
      "expected": "The spec fixes the I2C strapping as 'BS0 (pin 10) -> GND; BS1 (pin 11) -> VCC; BS2 (pin 12) -> GND' (BS[2:0]=010). BS0 must be tied to GND, not to VCC.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "BS0 (pin 10) -> GND; BS1 (pin 11) -> VCC; BS2 (pin 12) -> GND"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display sheet: BS0 pin 10 joins the VCC node shared with R4/R6/R7 pull-up tops, instead of a GND symbol"}
      ],
      "impact": "The SSD1306 is left in a non-I2C interface mode (SPI/parallel), so the MCU's DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA I2C bus cannot talk to the OLED; the display does not work.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing deviates from the reference in two places: the SWD programming header J1 has its SWDIO/SWCLK/SWO/RESET pins left unconnected (only VCC and GND are wired), and the OLED's BS0 strap pin is tied to VCC instead of GND, breaking the documented I2C interface selection."
}

